---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site } from "../../data/site";

// Terms of Service for Delve, Die, Repeat. Linked from /delve-die-repeat and
// used as the Terms URL on the Google Cloud OAuth consent screen. Privacy
// matters are covered by /privacy/apps; keep the two consistent.
const effective = "September 24, 2026";
const contact = "sheibeck@gmail.com";
---
<Layout
  title="Terms of Service — Delve, Die, Repeat"
  description="Terms of Service for Delve, Die, Repeat (delve-die-repeat), the offline Android roguelike from Darktier Studios."
  image="/assets/delve-die-repeat/og.jpg"
>
  <div class="container">
    <section style="padding:84px 0 28px">
      <p class="kicker">Delve, Die, Repeat · legal · terms</p>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(40px,6vw,72px);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0 0 0 -0.06em">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="privacy-meta">Effective {effective} · {site.legalName}, {site.location}</p>
    </section>

    <article class="privacy">
      <p class="privacy-lede">
        The short version: <strong>you buy the game once, you play it as much as you like, and your
        adventurers die a lot.</strong> That last part is a feature, not a defect, and it is not grounds for a
        refund.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Agreement</h2>
      <p>
        These terms govern your use of <strong>Delve, Die, Repeat</strong> (package
        <code>com.darktierstudios.delvedierepeat</code>, the “App”), published by {site.legalName} (“we”,
        “us”). By installing or using the App you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not
        use the App. Google Play's own
        <a href="https://play.google.com/about/play-terms/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Terms of Service</a>
        also apply to your purchase and download.
      </p>

      <h2>2. License</h2>
      <p>
        When you purchase the App through Google Play, we grant you a personal, non-exclusive,
        non-transferable, revocable license to install and use it on Android devices you own or control, for
        your own non-commercial entertainment. You may not copy, resell, redistribute, sublicense, decompile,
        or reverse-engineer the App, except where the law says you may. The App, its rules, text, art, music,
        and sounds, and the Mazeworld game it is based on, belong to {site.legalName} and remain ours.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Purchases and refunds</h2>
      <p>
        The App is a one-time paid purchase. It contains no ads and no in-app purchases. Payments, refunds,
        and family sharing are handled by Google Play under its refund policy; we do not process payments
        ourselves.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Gameplay, permadeath, and saves</h2>
      <p>
        Adventurers in the App die permanently, by design. Your runs, graveyard, records, and settings are
        stored only on your device. We cannot see, restore, or transfer them, and they are removed when you
        uninstall the App or clear its data. Lost progress, an unfair roll, or an especially rude epitaph are
        part of the game and are not defects.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Google Play Games sign-in and leaderboards</h2>
      <p>
        The App offers optional Google Play Games leaderboards through the in-game <strong>Compete</strong>
        setting. Signing in with Google Play Games is not required to play. When Compete is on, your Play
        Games profile name, avatar, and scores may be visible to other players under Google's rules. Your use
        of Google Play Games is governed by
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Terms of Service</a>
        and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Privacy Policy</a>.
        Please don't try to post scores by tampering with the App; we or Google may remove such scores.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        We collect no personal data and run no servers. What the App stores and what it sends to Google
        Play Games is described in our <a href="/privacy/apps">privacy policy for apps</a>; you can
        <a href="/privacy/delete-data">delete your leaderboard data</a> at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Updates</h2>
      <p>
        We may release updates that fix bugs, rebalance rules, or change features. Some updates may be
        needed for the App to keep working. We are not obligated to keep providing updates or support
        forever, though we would like to.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        The App is provided “as is” and “as available,” without warranties of any kind, express or implied,
        including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement, to the extent the
        law allows. We do not promise the App will be uninterrupted or error-free, or that the dice will ever
        be on your side.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, {site.legalName} is not liable for any indirect, incidental,
        special, consequential, or punitive damages, or any loss of data or progress, arising from your use
        of the App. Our total liability for any claim relating to the App will not exceed the amount you paid
        for it. Some jurisdictions do not allow these limits, so they may not all apply to you; nothing here
        limits rights you have under consumer protection law.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Termination</h2>
      <p>
        Your license ends automatically if you break these terms. You can end it at any time by uninstalling
        the App.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Michigan, USA, without regard to its conflict of
        law rules, except where your local consumer law requires otherwise.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        If we change these terms, the new version will be posted at this address with a new effective date.
        Continuing to use the App after a change means you accept the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a><br />
        {site.legalName} · {site.location} · <a href="/delve-die-repeat">Back to Delve, Die, Repeat</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
